// External owner portal over the Laasie loyalty data.
//
// This is the asset that answers Laasie's stated requirement for "easy-to-use embedded
// dashboard functionality for external web access": one declaration, dropped into their own
// web app as an iframe, carrying the dashboard, self-serve exploration and Ask AI — all three
// under the same row-level restriction rather than three separate integrations to secure.
//
// DATASET-LAYER SEPARATION:
// This portal reads `laasie_client`, a dataset that exists solely to carry the row-level
// restriction. Internal reporting reads the unscoped `laasie` dataset, so Laasie staff are
// never subject to client scoping and need no user attribute provisioned. The two audiences
// are separated at the dataset layer, not by per-user setup.
//
// SEPARATION OF INTERNAL AND EXTERNAL REPORTING:
// This portal exposes ONLY laasie_owner_portal. The internal dashboard
// (laasie_growth_performance) — cross-client growth, platform benchmarks, the stakeholder
// directory — is deliberately not listed here and is unreachable from the portal.
//
// ROW-LEVEL SECURITY:
// Enforced by the `owner_group_scope` permission on the `laasie_client` dataset
// (matches_user_attribute on `company_id` today — a demo-grade BORROWED attribute; see
// laasie_client.dataset.aml for why and for the upgrade path). It is listed in
// `required_permissions` so the portal FAILS CLOSED: a token that does not carry the scoping
// attribute is rejected outright, rather than falling through to every hotel group's revenue.
// The value to put on a stakeholder's token is their row in
// `public_external_stakeholders.owner_group_id`.
//
// COLUMN-LEVEL SECURITY:
// Because this portal exposes the dataset itself for exploration and Ask AI — not just a
// fixed dashboard — an external user can reach columns no widget displays. Guest and
// stakeholder email are therefore gated separately at the MODEL layer on `pii_access`, so a
// portal viewer without that attribute sees '(redacted)' no matter how they ask for it.
EmbedPortal laasie_portal {
  description: 'Laasie owner portal — a hotel owner or management company sees only the properties their own group operates, plus self-serve exploration and Ask AI over the same scoped data.'
  objects: [
    // Dashboards — external only
    laasie_owner_portal,
    // Datasets (self-serve exploration + AI, row-scoped by owner_group_scope)
    laasie_client,
  ]
  required_permissions: [
    laasie_client.permission.owner_group_scope,
  ]
  initial_object: 'ai'
  ai {
    customization {
      global {
        assistant_name: 'Laasie Insights'
      }
      chat_page {
        intro {
          header: 'Ask about your properties, your guests and how your rewards programme is performing.'
          body: @md
            ## 📈 Compare revenue, bookings and ADR against last year or last month
            ## 🏨 Break performance down by property, city or booking channel
            ## 🎁 See which rewards your guests actually claim, and what they cost
            ## 👥 Track loyalty tier mix and member booking rate over time
            ## 📌 Save any insight straight to your dashboard
          ;;
        }
        prompt_placeholder: 'e.g. How did revenue at my properties grow versus the same quarter last year?'
      }
    }
  }
}
